Bio: Creating a commercial website for renting equipment for sound engineers.

Project goals:

To get a commercial website for renting equipment for sound engineers.
Main tasks:

Implementation of a payment system.
Implementation of a user authorization system.
Development of an admin panel.
Product filtering.
Development of a contract for receiving goods for rent.
Implementation of a shopping cart.
Development of user accounts.
Technologies used:

MERN stack.
TailwindCSS.
Next.js using App Router.
Redux for state management.
Main tasks of the server part:

Implementation of API routes in Next.js.
Integration with a database (for example, MongoDB) via API routes.
Using server-side rendering (SSR) and static generation (SSG) to optimize performance and SEO.
Project stages:

Step-by-step work on the frontend.
Smooth transition to the backend.
Working with Next.js API routes for server logic.
Using built-in Next.js capabilities for server rendering and database integration.
Additional requirements:

The application must be in English.
Dark-toned design typical for sound engineers.
Fully responsive and modern component design using TailwindCSS.
Integration of Google fonts and Font Awesome icons for a better look.
Updated project structure for better component and style management.